# FairView API: the full loop, one click at a time.
# Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension. Click "Send Request" above each block, top to bottom.
# Tokens and ids are taken from earlier replies automatically: nothing needs to be copied.
#
# Before you start:
#   1. npm run seed -- --reset      (demo company, password123 for everyone)
#   2. DEV_OUTBOX=true in .env      (so step 10 can read the client's email)
#   3. npm run dev                  (and the ML service, for steps 15-16)

@base = http://localhost:5000/api

### 1. Rahul (manager) logs in
# @name rahul
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "rahul@fairview.test", "password": "password123" }

### 2. Priya (employee) logs in
# @name priya
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "priya@fairview.test", "password": "password123" }

### 3. Neha (HR) logs in
# @name hr
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "hr@fairview.test", "password": "password123" }

### 4. Rahul creates a project. The client is a contact, not a user: they will rate by email link.
# @name project
POST {{base}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{rahul.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Loyalty app", "client": { "name": "Mark Ellis", "email": "mark@shopwave.example", "company": "ShopWave" } }

### 5. Rahul gives Priya one piece of work (one owner per piece)
# @name task
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{rahul.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "projectId": "{{project.response.body.$._id}}", "employeeId": "{{priya.response.body.$.user.id}}", "title": "Points balance screen" }

### 6. Priya starts it
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{task.response.body.$._id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "in_progress" }

### 7. Priya submits it
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{task.response.body.$._id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "submitted", "submission": "https://github.com/example/pull/42" }

### 8. Rahul tries to deliver before rating -> 409 (he must rate first, blind)
POST {{base}}/tasks/{{task.response.body.$._id}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{rahul.response.body.$.token}}

### 9. Rahul rates it (2 stars), then delivers: the client gets a one-time rating link by email
POST {{base}}/tasks/{{task.response.body.$._id}}/rating
Authorization: Bearer {{rahul.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "score": 2, "comment": "Took longer than planned" }

###
POST {{base}}/tasks/{{task.response.body.$._id}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{rahul.response.body.$.token}}

### 10. Read the email the client would get (dev only) to find the link token
# @name outbox
GET {{base}}/dev/outbox

### 11. The client opens the link: sees the work and who built it, never the manager's score
GET {{base}}/public/rate/{{outbox.response.body.$[0].ratingToken}}

### 12. The client rates: 5 stars. No login. Locked at once.
POST {{base}}/public/rate/{{outbox.response.body.$[0].ratingToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "score": 5, "comment": "Clean and on time" }

### 13. Priya now sees both ratings on her work
# @name priyaTask
GET {{base}}/tasks/{{task.response.body.$._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{priya.response.body.$.token}}

### 14. Rahul tries to change the client's rating -> 403, and the attempt is logged
PATCH {{base}}/ratings/client/{{priyaTask.response.body.$.ratings.client.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{rahul.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "score": 1 }

### 15. HR runs the gap analysis (needs the ML service running and ML_URL set)
POST {{base}}/gap-cards/analyse
Authorization: Bearer {{hr.response.body.$.token}}

### 16. HR's Gap Cards: in the demo company, Rahul -> Priya and Sara -> Arjun
GET {{base}}/gap-cards?status=open
Authorization: Bearer {{hr.response.body.$.token}}

### 17. HR overview: client rating rate, per-manager averages, analysis status
GET {{base}}/insights/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{hr.response.body.$.token}}

### 18. HR audit log: the blocked edit from step 14 is here
GET {{base}}/insights/audit?outcome=blocked
Authorization: Bearer {{hr.response.body.$.token}}
